<title>UK: Results of Reuters UK smaller companies survey.</title>
<headline>Results of Reuters UK smaller companies survey.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are selected results of the 1997 Reuters survey of smaller companies investment research, sales and trading by fund manager (FM) and finance director (FD). It was carried out by Tempest Consulting.</p>
<p>Fund manager ranking of broker research  -- product and service</p>
<p>1. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson</p>
<p>2. Cazenove &amp; Co</p>
<p>3. SBC Warburg</p>
<p>4. UBS</p>
<p>5. ABN-AMRO Hoare Govett</p>
<p>6. BZW</p>
<p>7. Albert E Sharp</p>
<p>8. Merrill Lynch</p>
<p>9. NatWest Securities</p>
<p>10. Charterhouse Tilney</p>
<p>All sectors (broker research ranking by fund manager)</p>
<p>1. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson</p>
<p>2. UBS</p>
<p>3. SBC Warburg</p>
<p>All sectors (finance directors)</p>
<p>1. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson</p>
<p>2. HSBC James Capel</p>
<p>3. SBC Warburg</p>
<p> Top fund manager (FD)	   Top fund management group (FD)</p>
<p> 1. Andy Brough Schroder	 1. Schroder</p>
<p> 2. Mike Wetson Hermes	   2. Aberforth Partners</p>
<p> 3. David Warnock Aberforth    3. M&amp;G Group</p>
<p>Broker primary execution (FM) Broker secondary execution (FM)</p>
<p> 1. Cazenove			 1. UBS</p>
<p> 2. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson  2. Dresdner Kleinwort Benson</p>
<p> =3. UBS			     3. Cazenove</p>
<p> =3. SBC Warburg</p>
